","filename":"2025-0159-Response-from-HSE.pdf","promises":[{"id":1791,"quote":"HSE's Volunteering pages were published in October 2021, following extensive consultation with internal and external stakeholders. The guidance is meant to be broad and high level in scope, which is consistent with our guidance in other sectors, rather than focused on detailed advice for each sector in which volunteers employed. This allows for the guidance to cover the many organisations it applies to.","summary":"Publish a bulletin following the inquest findings","timescale":null},{"id":1792,"quote":"HSE's Engagement and Policy Division is currently going through a period of transition aimed at improving how we work and deliver outcomes, while continuing to deliver on our priorities as outlined within HSE's strategy HSE Strategy 2022 to 2032 - HSE. We will take your recommendations into consideration when we next review the volunteering pages of the guidance on our webpages.","summary":"Revise volunteering guidance to include comprehensive obligations for charitable trusts and voluntary organisations","timescale":null}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/joel-ineson-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Joel Ineson: Prevention of Future Deaths Report","date":"2025-04-10","coroner":"David Place","area":"Sunderland","ref":"2025-0183","categories":["Accident at Work and Health and Safety related deaths","Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-0183-Response-from-Department-for-Culture-Media-and-Sport-.pdf","filename":"2025-0183-Response-from-Department-for-Culture-Media-and-Sport-.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/2025-0183-Response-from-Health-and-Safety-Executive.pdf","filename":"2025-0183-Response-from-Health-and-Safety-Executive.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of